  "slug": "range-sum-query-2d-immutable",
  "title": "Range Sum Query 2D - Immutable",
  "difficulty": "Hard",
  "category": "Prefix sum",
  "patterns": [
    "prefix sum",
    "2d prefix sum"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "this is the 2D version of range sum query. what 1D idea (prefix sums, answering ranges via subtraction) generalizes here?",
    "build a prefix grid where prefix[r][c] holds the sum of every cell in the rectangle from (0,0) to (r-1,c-1)",
    "prefix[r][c] = matrix[r-1][c-1] + prefix[r-1][c] + prefix[r][c-1] - prefix[r-1][c-1] (the last term corrects for double-counting the overlap)",
    "for a query (row1,col1,row2,col2), the answer is prefix[row2+1][col2+1] - prefix[row1][col2+1] - prefix[row2+1][col1] + prefix[row1][col1] - the same inclusion-exclusion pattern, applied to look up the answer instead of build it"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "forgetting the inclusion-exclusion correction term when building or querying the prefix grid, causing double subtraction or double counting",
    "off-by-one between the 0-indexed matrix and a prefix grid that's one row/column larger to avoid boundary checks",
    "rebuilding the prefix grid or rescanning the rectangle for every query instead of precomputing once"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given a fixed 2D grid of integers and a batch of rectangle\nqueries. Each query is [row1, col1, row2, col2] (inclusive, 0-indexed),\ndescribing the top-left and bottom-right corners of a rectangle.\n\n**For every query, compute the sum of all elements inside that rectangle, and return all the answers in the same order as the queries.**\n\nThe grid never changes between queries.\n",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= matrix rows, matrix columns <= 200",
      "-10^5 <= matrix[i][j] <= 10^5",
      "0 <= row1 <= row2 < rows, 0 <= col1 <= col2 < cols",
      "0 <= queries.length <= 10^4"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "a query covering a single cell",
      "a query covering the entire grid",
      "a grid with only one row or one column"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
